#1423
book sorcery spell~
the Book of Sorcery~
A spellbook of some description lies abandoned on the ground.~
~
14 fg ao 0
0 0 0 0 0
5 3 400 50 0 1
E
book sorcery spell~
The book contains mostly blank pages but the &Wfirst&n and &Wsecond&n pages have
an ancient text scripted neatly.
~
E
one first~
Thus begins your study of spell magick. A good student binds into his
spellbook the preparation of each spell presented to him. A bold one commits
it to memory. And an impatient one throws the casting of the mind into the
world around him. While your path leads through the warring arts, you must
respect the ways of magick to master these practical spells.

In order to use the magick discussed below, the student must place a focus
within a circle of empowerment - the focus can be used at a later time to
recall the spell. A candle should be placed at each of the marked points
within the circle and the appropriate reagents placed in its center. A
specially prepared scroll must then be recited and the spell shall be bound
to the focus.

A warning to the young acolyte - once bound to a focus, the same spell
cannot be bound a second time - to do so would be a waste of precious
reagents.
~
E
two second~
&gIgnite Candle (utbuho qibmrog)&n
------------------------------
purified ash, pumice

&gEndure Heat (unsmecondus poih)&n
------------------------------
obsidian, pumice

&gSummon Daemon (gewbar miobar)&n
-----------------------------
purified ash, pumice, obsidian, daemon bone

&gBanish Daemon (vibugp miobar)&n
-----------------------------
purified ash, pumice, daemon bone
~
A
